        "object": "<ul><li><p>Russell clipped by Hamilton on lap one after power loss </p></li><li><p>British driver 50 points behind Antonelli in standings</p></li></ul><p>Toto Wolff, the Mercedes principal, has admitted the team let George Russell down at the Belgian Grand Prix. The British driver failed to score a point after a clash with Lewis Hamilton that Russell attributed to his car’s performance not being up to scratch.</p><p>The race <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/19/kimi-antonelli-f1-title-grip-belgian-grand-prix-george-russell-formula-one\">was won by Kimi Antonelli</a>, who now leads his teammate Russell by 50 points in the world championship, a serious blow to the latter’s title hopes.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/19/george-russell-toto-wolff-mercedes-lewis-hamilton-ferrari-belgian-grand-prix-f1-formule-one\">Continue reading...</a>"
